## What this slice builds

A standard-library checker at labs/colab-readiness-pass01. It reports six facets separately: transport_valid, runtime_dependencies_resolved, evidence_references_resolved, minimum_evidence_satisfied, smoke_result, and ready_for_declared_method. Missing, unknown, and not-run stay explicit. Exit 0 means a complete report was written. It does not mean ready. semantic_sufficiency stays not-established. The checker never executes source or return command text.

A separate fixture may run only snapshot bytes, plus the committed parser blob, in a disposable directory. That route is read, synthetic judgment, record, and reviewed re-read. It proves the checker against the accepted interface. It is not a correction of prime-cycle.

The inventory is for a future replay revision. This slice does not create that revision, a pass02 bundle, or a model rerun. It does not amend the first replay seal, source selection, results, or any historical subject. It does not change accepted tool digests, colab-support, the handoff checker, workflow consumers, kernel law, or 0036–0039.

## Failure policy, declared before use

Preserve the first failure. Default one underlying read-only diagnostic and one bounded named dependency check. No silent repair and no alternate tool. A manual fallback is labelled and cannot count as successful assisted execution. Further consequential ambiguity goes to Prime or the Director. Final counts name their cutoff. In-flight work stays in-flight. Unknown tokens, costs, and clocks stay unknown. Preparation effort is separate from the measured route.

